invariant: INV-7
file: handshake_parser.c
catches: webpki_session_test
reason: the parser takes a HelloRetryRequest whose key_share names x25519,
  a group the webpki hello already carried a share for, and the client
  answers it with a P-256 retry hello. RFC 9846 section 4.3.8 makes a retry
  naming a shared group an illegal_parameter at the retry itself, and a
  server could steer the client off the shares it sent onto a group it
  never asked for. secp256r1 is the one group the hello lists without a
  share (docs/decisions.md 63).

--- old
    if (rb_u16(e) != CH_GROUP_SECP256R1) {
        return CH_EPROTO;
    }
    info->retry_group = CH_GROUP_SECP256R1;
--- new
    uint16_t named = rb_u16(e);
    if (named != CH_GROUP_SECP256R1 && named != CH_GROUP_X25519) {
        return CH_EPROTO;
    }
    info->retry_group = CH_GROUP_SECP256R1;
